---
import octicons from '@primer/octicons';
import Entry from '../components/Entry.astro';
import Full from '../layouts/Full.astro';

const icon = (name: keyof typeof octicons, size = 16) => octicons[name].toSVG({ width: size, height: size });
---

<Full
	title="Games — Avior Studio"
	description="Play termcade in your terminal and Castle Drop in your browser, and meet Fianchetto, the chess card game in development at Avior Studio."
>
	<main id="main-content">
		<section class="page-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">
				<span></span> Games
			</p>
			<h1>
				Step into <em>another world.</em>
			</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Play the terminal arcade, or hold the castle wall in your browser. Fianchetto, a chess card game, is taking shape
				in the studio.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="game-gallery" aria-label="Art from our games">
			<a href="#termcade">
				<div class="gallery-termcade" aria-hidden="true">
					<span>▟▙</span>
					<b>▐▛▀▜▌</b>
					<span>▝▘ ▝▘</span>
				</div>
				<span>termcade · play now ↓</span>
			</a>
			<a href="#castle-drop">
				<img
					class="gallery-castle"
					src="/art/castledrop-fight.webp"
					alt="Castle Drop goblins marching on the castle wall past an archer tower"
					width="1280"
					height="720"
					loading="lazy"
				/>
				<span>Castle Drop · play now ↓</span>
			</a>
			<a href="#fianchetto">
				<img
					class="gallery-fianchetto"
					src="/art/fianchetto-queen.webp"
					alt="Fianchetto's ivory queen, crowned in gold, between candles"
					width="445"
					height="443"
					loading="lazy"
				/>
				<span>Fianchetto · in development ↓</span>
			</a>
		</section>
		<section class="entries">
			<Entry
				name="termcade"
				id="termcade"
				tagline="A terminal arcade"
				status="Playable now"
				available={true}
				meta="Rust · Ratatui · Wasmtime"
				command="termcade"
				commandNote="Install a verified release; use a truecolor terminal at 80×24 or larger"
				links={[{ href: 'https://github.com/aviorstudio/termcade', label: 'Source on GitHub' }]}
			>
				<p>
					Classic games rendered at sub-cell resolution with block pixels, so a terminal cell becomes a 2×2 or 2×3 grid
					of pixels and the playfield gets sharper than the font should allow. It ships with Asteroid, Tetris and
					Brickough, playable offline the moment it starts.
				</p>
				<p>
					The arcade compiles no games into itself. Every game is a sandboxed WebAssembly package running under Wasmtime
					with no filesystem and no network, so a broken one shows up dimmed on the menu with its reason rather than
					taking the arcade down. The same binary is the dev kit: <code>termcade dev new you/mygame</code> scaffolds
					one, <code>termcade dev build</code>
					packages it, and anyone can publish for players to <code>termcade add</code>.
				</p>
			</Entry>

			<Entry
				name="Castle Drop"
				id="castle-drop"
				tagline="A card-driven castle defense"
				status="Playable now"
				available={true}
				meta="Godot 4 · browser game"
				links={[{ href: 'https://castledrop.avior.studio', label: 'Play in your browser' }]}
			>
				<p>
					Goblins march down the rows of a five-by-nine field toward your castle wall, and a hand of cards refills as the
					fight goes on. Build cards raise archer, mage, artillery, wall and workshop towers on the tiles and level them
					up; ability cards fire every tower of a kind near the spot you choose; spells like Gust, Snare and Pitfall deal
					with goblins too heavy to lift. The rest you can still grab and throw.
				</p>
				<p>
					Fights string together into a run across lands, each mapped like a roguelike, with elites, merchants, events and
					rest stops on the way to the land's giant. Win a fight to add a card to your deck; gold from kills builds towers
					and buys cards, and towers stand for the whole run. The towers, goblins and backdrops are painted, then animated
					as cut-out puppets.
				</p>
			</Entry>

			<Entry
				name="Fianchetto"
				id="fianchetto"
				tagline="A chess card game"
				status="In development"
				meta="Godot 4 · Rust rules core · private repository"
			>
				<p>
					Every fight starts with your king alone on the board. Summon pieces and cast spells from a hand of cards, with
					mana that grows by one each turn, then move each of your pieces once. Capture the enemy king to win; lose yours
					and the fight is over. The enemy plays by the same rules, with its own deck, mana and pieces.
				</p>
				<p>
					Two modes on one device: Gambit, a roguelike run of three fights where each win adds a card to your deck, and
					Normal, where you build a twenty-card deck and face the computer opponent of your choice. The rules live in a
					shared Rust core, laid out for a phone held upright like a chess app.
				</p>
			</Entry>


		</section>

		<section class="aside-note">
			<p>
				Fianchetto and Castle Drop run on the studio's own devtools — gdam pins the addons they share, gdlint checks
				the GDScript.
			</p>
			<a class="ghost-cta" href="/devtools">
				See the devtools <span class="icon" set:html={icon('arrow-right', 13)} />
			</a>
		</section>
	</main>
</Full>

<style>
	.game-gallery {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px));
		margin: 0 auto 70px;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 20px;
	}
	.game-gallery > a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration: none;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}
	.game-gallery > a > img,
	.gallery-castle,
	.gallery-termcade {
		height: 320px;
		width: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: center 40%;
	}
	.game-gallery > a > span {
		font: 11px var(--mono);
		padding: 18px 0;
	}
	.gallery-termcade {
		background: var(--ink-deep);
		border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		color: var(--paper);
		font: 56px/1 var(--mono);
	}
	.gallery-termcade b {
		font-weight: 400;
	}
	.gallery-castle {
		object-position: 22% 50%;
	}
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.game-gallery {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.game-gallery > a > img,
		.gallery-castle,
		.gallery-termcade {
			height: 350px;
		}
	}

	.page-hero {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px));
		margin: 60px auto 70px;
	}
	.eyebrow {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 9px;
		margin: 0 0 22px;
		color: var(--quiet);
		font: 620 11px/1 var(--mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	.eyebrow span {
		width: 7px;
		height: 7px;
		border-radius: 1px;
		background: var(--seal);
	}
	/* Narrow enough that the line breaks where the sentence does, between the
		   roman half and the italic one, instead of mid-phrase. */
	h1 {
		max-width: 640px;
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--bone);
		font-size: clamp(42px, 5.4vw, 68px);
		font-weight: 590;
		line-height: 0.99;
		letter-spacing: -0.058em;
	}
	h1 em {
		color: var(--quiet);
		font-family: var(--serif);
		font-weight: 400;
	}
	.lede {
		max-width: 620px;
		margin: 28px 0 0;
		color: var(--quiet);
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.entries {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px));
		margin: 0 auto 90px;
	}

	.aside-note {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px));
		margin: 0 auto 40px;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 40px;
		border-radius: 10px;
		background: var(--raised);
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		padding: 34px 40px;
	}
	.aside-note p {
		max-width: 640px;
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--quiet);
		font-size: 14.5px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}
	.ghost-cta {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 7px;
		flex: none;
		color: var(--paper);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
		padding: 6px 0;
		font-size: 13px;
		font-weight: 650;
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.ghost-cta:hover {
		border-bottom-color: var(--paper);
	}

	@media (max-width: 980px) {
		.aside-note {
			align-items: flex-start;
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 22px;
		}
	}
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.page-hero,
		.entries,
		.aside-note {
			width: min(100% - 28px, 1180px);
		}
		.page-hero {
			margin: 36px auto 50px;
		}
		h1 {
			font-size: clamp(36px, 11.5vw, 52px);
		}
		.lede {
			margin-top: 22px;
			font-size: 15px;
		}
		.aside-note {
			padding: 26px 24px;
		}
		.aside-note p {
			font-size: 13.5px;
		}
	}

	h1 {
		font: 400 clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px) / 1.04 var(--serif);
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--bone);
	}
	h1 em {
		font-style: italic;
	}
	.entry-list {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
	}
</style>
